WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.912 --> 00:00:03.980
(gaming music)

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.033
- [Narrator] Crawling
through underground pipes.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.063
Racing to catch a mushroom.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.523
And saving Princess Peach.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.333
All things you did in
the Mushroom Kingdom.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.910
You might think you know
everything about your favorite

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.530
high-pitched, turtle-
squashing, Italian plumber but,

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.549
you have no idea.

00:00:26.549 --> 00:00:29.132
(gaming music)

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.943
Let's start from the
beginning, the very beginning.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.580
Guess when Nintendo was founded.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.763
In the 19th century, 1889 to be exact.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.740
They started out as
playing cards manufacturer

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.670
and, as years passed, expanded
their lines of products.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.023
Going from toys to instant
rice and even taxi services.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.210
Fast forward to the 1970s, the company is

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.300
in dire financial straights and is looking

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.970
to reinvent itself. With the
golden age of video games

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:14.310
in full swing, Nintendo saw an
opportunity to join the fray.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:18.430
So, they entrusted a young
artist to lead their initiative.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.033
A man that would ultimately
change video games forever.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.010
This is Shigeru Miyamoto,
the world famous creator

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.530
of the world famous character

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.150
- [Shigeru] Mario.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.550
- [Narrator] And this is
how Mario got his look.

00:01:37.552 --> 00:01:41.969
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.828
- [Narrator] But that was
quite a challenge in 8-bit.

00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:03.630
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.304
- [Narrator] And one thing let to another.

00:02:05.304 --> 00:02:09.721
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.266
- [Narrator] Now our
character needed, well, a name.

00:02:24.266 --> 00:02:28.683
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.726
- [Narrator] That video
game was Donkey Kong.

00:02:32.726 --> 00:02:37.143
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:02:39.499 --> 00:02:42.183
- [Narrator] And that silly
hero had a signature move.

00:02:42.183 --> 00:02:46.600
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.740
- [Narrator] Mr. Video become Jumpman,

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.680
a carpenter climbing ladders
on a construction site.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.557
But, he needed a more relatable name.

00:02:56.557 --> 00:03:00.974
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.932
- [Narrator] To a warehouse
in Seattle to be precise.

00:03:14.932 --> 00:03:16.313
And what happened there?

00:03:16.313 --> 00:03:20.730
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.670
- [Narrator] That
landlord was Mario Segale,

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.438
and he looked like this, with a mustache.

00:03:30.438 --> 00:03:31.570
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:34.420
- [Narrator] Wait, so that
guy inspired Mario's name?

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.837
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.100
- [Narrator] So, we had a funny idea:

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.440
We wanted to look for Mario Segale.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.970
That elusive landlord,
turns out he still lives

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:51.580
in the Seattle area, and
he's still in real estate.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.340
In fact, he's quite a mogul.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.830
His name is even on a street sign.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.720
We tried to call him to ask about Mario,

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.920
but he didn't want to
comment on the matter.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.963
What happened in that warehouse
stays in that warehouse.

00:04:03.963 --> 00:04:06.563
(Mario sound effects)

00:04:06.563 --> 00:04:09.850
- After Donkey Kong, our
hero was ready to be a star

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.963
on his own, so Miyomoto set out
to design him his own world.

00:04:15.507 --> 00:04:19.924
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.300
- [Narrator] Mario was jumping over pipes.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.507
So naturally, he became a plumber.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:35.097
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.950
- [Narrator] Instead,
Mario was kind of a chubby,

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:41.005
blue collar hero.

00:04:41.005 --> 00:04:45.422
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.320
- [Narrator] And players
got to enjoy even more

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.597
of Mario with his doppelgänger.

00:04:53.597 --> 00:04:58.014
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:05:01.288 --> 00:05:04.108
- [Narrator] Like Mario,
his name has quite a story.

00:05:04.108 --> 00:05:08.450
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.849
- [Narrator] And it was meant to be.

00:05:09.849 --> 00:05:14.270
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.920
- [Narrator] Although the
Mario brothers have a lot

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.450
in common, Mario, he
remained the true star.

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.749
And ultimately, he's more
than a video game character.

00:05:22.749 --> 00:05:27.166
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.850
- [Narrator] We see him
pretty much everywhere.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.843
But, we'll never look at the
Nintendo mascot the same way.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.814
Mario is a legend, and so is his creator.

00:05:40.814 --> 00:05:45.231
(Shigeru speaks in foreign language)

00:05:47.064 --> 00:05:50.341
(gaming music)

00:05:50.341 --> 00:05:52.661
- [Mario] Yi-hoo-hoo.

00:05:52.661 --> 00:05:54.661
(chime)

